error: /mnt is not a volume of its own: it is stored on a network block device, which a program can serve from a file on this computer's own disk. Nothing was written.
  Use a volume on a disk or partition of its own, or an encrypted volume opened from one: only such a volume can be told apart from this computer's own storage.
  If the device keeps its data on storage this computer does not use, read "Where setup happens" in the operator guide on another device: opening it here leaves traces such as ~/.lesshst.
